{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Return on Investment.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Return on Investment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"return on investment return on investment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Return on Investment.md","fileName":"Return on Investment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Return on Investment","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 22:42\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Big Data Project Value Management]] [[Cloud Business Value and Finance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Data Project Value Management","Cloud Business Value and Finance","Net Present Value","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","cloudcomputing_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Return on Investment.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Return on Investment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"return on investment return on investment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Return on Investment.md","fileName":"Return on Investment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Return on Investment","heading":"Return on Investment","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Return on investment compares the financial benefit produced by an initiative with the capital committed to it. For a big-data project, value comes from improved decisions, lower cost, new revenue, or faster processes rather than the quantity of data collected.\n\nTiming, risk, dependencies, and the opportunity to fund a different project make simple benefit-minus-cost totals incomplete.\n\nA basic calculation expresses ROI as the gain from an investment minus its cost, divided by that cost. When gains and costs occur at different times, an adjusted comparison should use [[Net Present Value]] rather than treating every cash flow as if it occurred immediately.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Dat